  "term": "L-dopa",
  "definition": "L-dopa, also called levodopa, is the naturally occurring form of dihydroxyphenylalanine and a direct precursor of dopamine. Unlike dopamine, it can be taken by mouth and cross into the brain, where nerve cells convert it to dopamine; it is used in treating parkinsonian disorders.",
